(4852098, 704473, 41337, '<td valign="top">Interesting twist to the shot. Not a bad effort. You just need to polish it up a bit. <br/> <br/>For starters don''t light it from above or in the front that causes those reflections that are not appealling. Instead find a way to light it from the back, bounce the light if you have to, narrow the beam if you''re getting some light spilling in the front and causing reflections. <br/> <br/>What makes this concept in particular appealing is the clean lines that you normally see in these shots. Your line is not straight. That''s harder to do if you have the paper running under the glass so you may want to not do that. <br/> <br/>Lastly, it could use a better title. For example, something like "Limon" (fusion of the two) might have gotten you some extra points. <br/> <br/>Anyway, just some thoughts. Good luck!</td>', 'Interesting twist to the shot. Not a bad effort. You just need to polish it up a bit.  For starters don''t light it from above or in the front that causes those reflections that are not appealling. Instead find a way to light it from the back, bounce the light if you have to, narrow the beam if you''re getting some light spilling in the front and causing reflections.  What makes this concept in particular appealing is the clean lines that you normally see in these shots. Your line is not straight. That''s harder to do if you have the paper running under the glass so you may want to not do that.  Lastly, it could use a better title. For example, something like "Limon" (fusion of the two) might have gotten you some extra points.  Anyway, just some thoughts. Good luck!', '2008-07-30 21:32:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(4852102, 704005, 41337, '<td valign="top">Clean lines. Good lighting. Just needs a new twist to make it your own.</td>', 'Clean lines. Good lighting. Just needs a new twist to make it your own.', '2008-07-30 21:33:58.000000', NULL, 1),
