(4886026, 702989, 30982, '<td valign="top">Dude, you were really, really robbed on this.  One of the few actual still lifes in the challenge, and very masterfully done.  Lovely.</td>', 'Dude, you were really, really robbed on this.  One of the few actual still lifes in the challenge, and very masterfully done.  Lovely.', '2008-08-13 14:50:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4889342, 703550, 15163, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DarkRider:</b></div><hr/><i> Low scoring shot for me...if you would like an honest critique of this photo please PM me. Best of luck. Scott </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Would appreciate an honest critique.<br/> <br/>Thanks<br/>Larry</td>', 'Originally posted by DarkRider: Low scoring shot for me...if you would like an honest critique of this photo please PM me. Best of luck. Scott   Would appreciate an honest critique. ThanksLarry', '2008-08-14 20:31:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4891162, 704349, 59029, '<td valign="top">A very underestimated shot.  I love the child''s arms up in the air in the bg and you leaving all work-related paraphernalia on the table...cellphone, car keys etc.  well done!</td>', 'A very underestimated shot.  I love the child''s arms up in the air in the bg and you leaving all work-related paraphernalia on the table...cellphone, car keys etc.  well done!', '2008-08-15 22:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4896331, 704218, 48228, '<td valign="top">This is so fresh, and just a lovely still life.....</td>', 'This is so fresh, and just a lovely still life.....', '2008-08-18 22:13:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4896418, 704218, 68166, '<td valign="top">good title for great still life<br/>great color, light and shadows<br/>well done</td>', 'good title for great still lifegreat color, light and shadowswell done', '2008-08-18 23:00:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4903618, 704006, 69008, '<td valign="top">It''s hard to tell about the file size in this shot, but it looks like it may have been shot with the camera set to lower resolution than it would be normally, i/e set at 1meg instead of 6 or 8 meg. In particular, the edges of the court line, and the lettering on the racket look a little pixilated to me. <br/>With this Mac, I can see all the tones in the darker areas, but some computer screens would not show the low key areas, which would affect the voting.  I found my monitor set at the std Mac gamma, which is brighter than almost all PC''s screens. It made my photos dark looking for everyone else until I set my monitor to 1.8 gamma. <br/>The composition includes lines, curves, and squares which is nice, and depth of field is good.  The placement in the composition, centered, just does not seem quite exciting enough to do well in a challenge. <br/>Don''t be discouraged, just keep shooting and look at a lot of the images that are doing well, and you will soon have some good scores. <br/>Happy first comment!  : )</td>', 'It''s hard to tell about the file size in this shot, but it looks like it may have been shot with the camera set to lower resolution than it would be normally, i/e set at 1meg instead of 6 or 8 meg. In particular, the edges of the court line, and the lettering on the racket look a little pixilated to me. With this Mac, I can see all the tones in the darker areas, but some computer screens would not show the low key areas, which would affect the voting.  I found my monitor set at the std Mac gamma, which is brighter than almost all PC''s screens. It made my photos dark looking for everyone else until I set my monitor to 1.8 gamma. The composition includes lines, curves, and squares which is nice, and depth of field is good.  The placement in the composition, centered, just does not seem quite exciting enough to do well in a challenge. Don''t be discouraged, just keep shooting and look at a lot of the images that are doing well, and you will soon have some good scores. Happy first comment!  : )', '2008-08-21 23:01:35.000000', NULL, 0);
